Minimum area: 2 mm x 2 mm (footprint 30 m x 30 m).</description><area_symbol inner_color="34" min_area="1125" patterns="2"><pattern type="2" angle="1.5708" rotatable="true" line_spacing="2550" line_offset="0" offset_along_line="0" point_distance="2850"><symbol type="1" code="" name="Pattern fill 1"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="0" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="29" line_width="300" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">0 -975;0 975;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></pattern><pattern type="2" angle="1.5708" rotatable="true" line_spacing="2550" line_offset="1275" offset_along_line="1425" point_distance="2850"><symbol type="1" code="" name="Pattern fill 2"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1500" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="29" line_width="300" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">0 -975;0 975;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></pattern></area_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="100" code="415" name="Distinct cultivation boundary"><description>A boundary of cultivated land vegetation (symbols 401, 412, 413, 414) or a boundary between areas of cultivated land when not shown with other symbols (fence, wall, path, etc.).
Minimum length: 2 mm (footprint 30 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="210" minimum_length="3000" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="101" code="416" name="Distinct vegetation boundary"><description>A distinct forest edge or vegetation boundary within the forest.
Very distinct forest edges and vegetation boundaries may be represented using the cultivation boundary symbol. Only one of the vegetation boundary symbols (black dotted line or dashed green line) can be used on a map. For areas with a lot of rock features, it is recommended to use the green dashed line for vegetation boundaries.
A disadvantage with a green line is that it cannot be used to show distinct vegetation boundaries around and within symbol Vegetation: fight (410). An alternative for these situations is to use symbol Distinct cultivation boundary (415).
Minimum length, black dot implementation: 5 dots (2.5 mm - footprint 37 m).
Minimum length, green line implementation: 4 dashes (1.8 mm - footprint 27 m).</description><line_symbol color="-1" line_width="0" minimum_length="330" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="675" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="8" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="8" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><mid_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Mid symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="165" inner_color="2" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol></mid_symbol></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="102" code="416.1" name="Distinct vegetation boundary, green dashed line"><description>A distinct forest edge or vegetation boundary within the forest.
Very distinct forest edges and vegetation boundaries may be represented using the cultivation boundary symbol. Only one of the vegetation boundary symbols (black dotted line or dashed green line) can be used on a map. For areas with a lot of rock features, it is recommended to use the green dashed line for vegetation boundaries.
A disadvantage with a green line is that it cannot be used to show distinct vegetation boundaries around and within symbol Vegetation: fight (410). An alternative for these situations is to use symbol Distinct cultivation boundary (415).
Minimum length, black dot implementation: 5 dots (2.5 mm - footprint 37 m).
Minimum length, green line implementation: 4 dashes (1.8 mm - footprint 27 m).</description><line_symbol color="25" line_width="210" minimum_length="2700" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="450" break_length="300" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="103" code="417" name="Prominent large tree"><description>Footprint: 13.5 m x 13.5 m.</description><point_symbol inner_radius="405" inner_color="-1" outer_width="270" outer_color="3" elements="1"><element><symbol type="1" code=""><point_symbol inner_radius="825" inner_color="22" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol><object type="0"><coords count="1">0 0;</coords></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="104" code="418" name="Prominent bush or tree"><description>Use sparingly, as it is easily mistaken for symbol Small knoll (109).
Footprint: 9.0 m x 9.0 m.</description><point_symbol inner_radius="75" inner_color="22" outer_width="300" outer_color="3" elements="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="105" code="419" name="Prominent vegetation feature"><description>The symbol is orientated to north.
The definition of the symbol must be given on the map.
Footprint: 13.5 m x 13.5 m.</description><point_symbol inner_radius="1500" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="4"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="3" line_width="270" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">-585 -585;585 585;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="3" line_width="270" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">585 -585;-585 585;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="22" line_width="540" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">-675 -675;675 675;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="22" line_width="540" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">675 -675;-675 675;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="106" code="501" name="Paved area, with bounding line"><description>An area with a firm surface such as asphalt, hard gravel, tiles, concrete or the like. Paved areas should be bordered (or framed) by a thin black line where they have a distinct boundary.
Minimum area: 1 mm x 1 mm (footprint 15 m x 15 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part private="true"><symbol type="4" code="501.1" name="Paved area (Lower Brown 50%)"><description>An area with a firm level surface such as asphalt, hard gravel, tiles, concrete or the like.</description><area_symbol inner_color="13" min_area="1125" patterns="0"/></symbol></part><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="501.2" name="Paved area, bounding line (below Upper Brown 50%)"><line_symbol color="12" line_width="210" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="4" id="107" code="501.1" name="Paved area"><description>An area with a firm surface such as asphalt, hard gravel, tiles, concrete or the like. Paved areas should be bordered (or framed) by a thin black line where they have a distinct boundary.
Minimum area: 1 mm x 1 mm (footprint 15 m x 15 m).</description><area_symbol inner_color="11" min_area="1125" patterns="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="108" code="501.2" name="Paved area, bounding line"><description>Paved areas should be bordered (or framed) by a thin black line where they have a distinct boundary.</description><line_symbol color="8" line_width="210" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="109" code="502" name="Wide road, minimum width"><description>The width should be drawn to scale, but not smaller than the minimum width (0.3 + 2*0.14 mm - footprint 8.7 m). The outer boundary lines may be replaced with other black line symbols, such as symbol Fence (516), Impassable fence (518), Wall (513) or Impassable wall (515) if the feature is so close to the road edge that it cannot practically be shown as a separate symbol.
The space between the black lines is filled with brown (50%).
A road with two carriageways can be represented using two wide road symbols side by side, keeping only one of the road edges in the middle.</description><line_symbol color="11" line_width="450" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="14" width="210" shift="105"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="110" code="502.2" name="Road with two carriageways"><description>The width should be drawn to scale, but not smaller than the minimum width (0.3 + 2*0.14 mm - footprint 8.7 m). The outer boundary lines may be replaced with other black line symbols, such as symbol Fence (516), Impassable fence (518), Wall (513) or Impassable wall (515) if the feature is so close to the road edge that it cannot practically be shown as a separate symbol.
The space between the black lines is filled with brown (50%).
A road with two carriageways can be represented using two wide road symbols side by side, keeping only one of the road edges in the middle.</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="501.1" name="Motorway, outer part"><line_symbol color="13" line_width="1170" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="14" width="210" shift="105"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol></part><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="501.2" name="Motorway, inner part"><line_symbol color="12" line_width="210" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="11" width="480" shift="240"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="111" code="503" name="Road"><description>A maintained road suitable for motor vehicles in all weather. Width less than 5 m.</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="525" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="112" code="504" name="Vehicle track"><description>A track or poorly maintained road suitable for vehicles only when travelling slowly. For distinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are joined at the junction.
For indistinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are not joined.
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (6.25 mm - footprint 94 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="525" minimum_length="9375" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="4500" break_length="375" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="113" code="505" name="Footpath"><description>An easily runnable path, bicycle track or old vehicle track.
For distinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are joined at the junction.
For indistinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are not joined.
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (4.25 mm - footprint 64 m)</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="375" minimum_length="6375" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="3000" break_length="375" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="114" code="506" name="Small footpath"><description>A runnable small path or (temporary) forest extraction track which can be followed at competition speed.
For distinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are joined at the junction.
For indistinct junctions the dashes of the symbols are not joined.
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (2.25 mm - footprint 34 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="270" minimum_length="3375" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1500" break_length="375" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="115" code="507" name="Less distinct small footpath"><description>A runnable less distinct / visible small path or forestry extraction track.
Minimum length: two sections of double dashes (5.3 mm - footprint 79.5 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="270" minimum_length="7950" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1500" break_length="1200" dashes_in_group="2" in_group_break_length="375" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="116" code="508" name="Narrow ride"><description>A forest ride or a prominent trace (forestry extraction track, sandy track, ski track) through the terrain which does not have a distinct runnable path along it. Runnability is shown using a slightly thicker line of yellow, green or white as background.
Without background: the same runnability as the surroundings.
Yellow 100%: easy running.
White in green: normal runnability.
Green 30%: slow running.
Green 60%: walk.
Minimum length: two dashes (3.25 mm - footprint 48 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="210" minimum_length="4875" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="3000" break_length="375" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="117" code="508.1" name="Narrow ride, easy running"><description>A forest ride or a prominent trace (forestry extraction track, sandy track, ski track) through the terrain which does not have a distinct runnable path along it. Runnability is shown using a slightly thicker line of yellow, green or white as background.
Minimum length: two dashes (3.25 mm - footprint 48 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="116"/><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="508.1.1" name="Yellow background"><line_symbol color="19" line_width="675" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="118" code="508.2" name="Narrow ride, normal runnability"><description>A forest ride or a prominent trace (forestry extraction track, sandy track, ski track) through the terrain which does not have a distinct runnable path along it. Runnability is shown using a slightly thicker line of yellow, green or white as background.
Minimum length: two dashes (3.25 mm - footprint 48 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="116"/><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="508.4.1" name="White background"><line_symbol color="22" line_width="675" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="119" code="508.3" name="Narrow ride, slow running"><description>A forest ride or a prominent trace (forestry extraction track, sandy track, ski track) through the terrain which does not have a distinct runnable path along it. Runnability is shown using a slightly thicker line of yellow, green or white as background.
Minimum length: two dashes (3.25 mm - footprint 48 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="116"/><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="508.2.1" name="Green 20% background"><line_symbol color="21" line_width="675" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="120" code="508.4" name="Narrow ride, walk"><description>A forest ride or a prominent trace (forestry extraction track, sandy track, ski track) through the terrain which does not have a distinct runnable path along it. Runnability is shown using a slightly thicker line of yellow, green or white as background.
Minimum length: two dashes (3.25 mm - footprint 48 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="116"/><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="508.3.1" name="Green 50% background"><line_symbol color="20" line_width="675" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="121" code="509" name="Railway"><description>A railway or other kind of railed track.
If it is forbidden to run along the railway, it shall be combined with symbol Out-of-bounds route (711). If it is forbidden to cross the railway, it must be combined with symbol Area that shall not be entered (520) or Out-of-bounds area (709).
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (4 mm - footprint 60 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="509.0.1" name="Railway helper: inner black dashes"><line_symbol color="2" line_width="525" minimum_length="6000" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="2250" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="509.0.2" name="Railway, Black background"><line_symbol color="4" line_width="525" minimum_length="6000" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="2250" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="2" width="150" shift="0"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="122" code="510" name="Power line, cableway or skilift"><description>Power line, cableway or skilift. The bars show the exact location of the pylons. The line may be broken to improve legibility.
If a section of a power line, cableway or skilift goes along a road or path (and does not offer significant additional navigational value) it should be omitted.
Minimum length (isolated): 5 mm (footprint: 75 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="210" minimum_length="7500" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><dash_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Dash symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1500" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="2" line_width="210" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">0 -555;0 555;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></dash_symbol></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="123" code="511" name="Major power line, minimum width"><description>Major power lines should be drawn with a double line. The gap between the lines may indicate the extent of the power line. The lines may be broken to improve legibility.
